{
  "name": "What Happens During Basement Door Installation?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Thinking about a new basement door? You're probably curious about what the installation process actually looks like. It's more than just slapping a door into a hole; there are some key steps HH Remodeling LLC takes to ensure a secure and weather-tight fit.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2",
      "text": "Phase 1: Preparation and Framing. We'll start by carefully measuring and squaring up the door frame. If it's a new opening, this phase might involve some careful cutting and structural adjustments, which is where professional experience really counts. This ensures the door has a perfectly plumb and level opening to sit in.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3",
      "text": "Phase 2: Anchoring the Frame. Next, we securely drill anchors directly into your masonry or concrete foundation. This isn't a step to rush; proper fastening prevents movement and ensures the door stays put, resisting wear and tear for years to come. We make sure it's firmly attached and aligned.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4",
      "text": "Phase 3: Sealing and Adjustments. Once the frame is anchored, we move on to critical sealing. Caulking all seams thoroughly is essential to prevent water intrusion and drafts. We also fine-tune any springs or gas assistance mechanisms. This ensures the door is perfectly counterbalanced—it shouldn't slam shut on its own or fly open unexpectedly. This attention to detail makes all the difference in functionality and longevity. If you're considering a new basement door, give us a call at 303-505-0866!",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
